meta {
  name: 05 QA Test Cases
  seq: 5
}

docs {
  # QA test cases for the Task API
  One request = one test case. Names say what is tested and the expected result.
  Each request's Docs tab holds the test case ID, the requirement, steps and expected result.

  Tags: smoke (quick check), regression (everything), negative, boundary.
  TC-00 and TC-02 carry every tag, because the other tests need fresh data and a token.

  Run from the terminal:
    bru run "05 QA Test Cases" --env Local --tags smoke
    bru run "05 QA Test Cases" --env Local --tags negative,boundary
    bru run "05 QA Test Cases" --env Local --reporter-html qa-report.html
}
